body:
## Problem

  @cashu/cashu-ts Token supports an optional memo, but Coco’s send operation API does not currently provide a way to attach that memo before the token is persisted.

  As a result, callers can only add memo to the returned token object after send.execute(...) completes. That can make the immediate in-memory result look correct, but
  the persisted send operation/history projection still contains the original token without memo.

  ## Relevant Code

  Token supports memo?: string:
```
  // @cashu/cashu-ts
  export type Token = {
    mint: string;
    proofs: Proof[];
    memo?: string;
    unit?: string;
  };
```
  Send history entries already expose the persisted token:
```
  // packages/core/models/History.ts
  export type SendHistoryEntry = OperationHistoryBase & {
    type: 'send';
    amount: Amount;
    state: SendHistoryState;
    token?: Token;
  };
```
  The send history projection reads token from the persisted send operation:
```
  // packages/core/models/History.ts
  export function projectSendOperation(operation: SendOperation): SendHistoryEntry | null {
    // ...
    const token = 'token' in prepared ? prepared.token : undefined;

    return {
      // ...
      ...(token ? { token } : {}),
    };
  }
```
  The public send execution API currently accepts only the operation/id:
```
  // packages/core/api/SendOpsApi.ts
  async execute(
    operationOrId: SendOperation | string,
  ): Promise<{ operation: PendingSendOperation; token: Token }>

  SendOperationService.execute(...) persists the pending operation before callers can mutate the returned token:

  // packages/core/operations/send/SendOperationService.ts
  const result = await handler.execute(ctx);

  if (result.status === 'PENDING') {
    await this.sendOperationRepository.update(result.pending);
    pending = result.pending;
    token = result.token ?? null;
  }
```
  The default and P2PK handlers both create a token and put it on the pending operation:
```
  const token: Token = {
    mint: mintUrl,
    proofs: sendProofs,
    unit: operation.unit,
  };

  const pending: PendingSendOperation = {
    ...operation,
    state: 'pending',
    updatedAt: Date.now(),
    token,
  };
```
  The SQLite repositories persist that operation token through tokenJson:
```
  // packages/expo-sqlite/src/repositories/SendOperationRepository.ts
  // packages/sqlite3/src/repositories/SendOperationRepository.ts
  function serializeToken(operation: SendOperation): string | null {
    const maybeTokenOperation = operation as SendOperation & { token?: unknown };
    return maybeTokenOperation.token ? JSON.stringify(maybeTokenOperation.token) : null;
  }
```
  The history repository later reads tokenJson back into the send history entry:
```
  // packages/expo-sqlite/src/repositories/HistoryRepository.ts
  case 'send': {
    const token = parseToken(row.tokenJson);

    return {
      ...base,
      type: 'send',
      state: row.state as HistoryEntry['state'],
      ...(token ? { token } : {}),
    } as HistoryEntry;
  }
```
  ## Proposed Fix

  Add optional send-token metadata support to the send execution path, starting with memo.

  Suggested API:
```
  // packages/core/api/SendOpsApi.ts
  export interface ExecuteSendOptions {
    memo?: string;
  }

  async execute(
    operationOrId: SendOperation | string,
    options?: ExecuteSendOptions,
  ): Promise<{ operation: PendingSendOperation; token: Token }> {
    const operation = await this.resolveOperation(operationOrId);
    // existing state check...
    return this.sendOperationService.execute(operation, options);
  }
```
  Thread the options into the service:
```
  // packages/core/operations/send/SendOperationService.ts
  export interface ExecuteSendOptions {
    memo?: string;
  }

  function normalizeMemo(memo: string | undefined): string | undefined {
    const trimmed = memo?.trim();
    return trimmed && trimmed.length > 0 ? trimmed : undefined;
  }

  function applyTokenMemo(token: Token | undefined, memo: string | undefined): Token | undefined {
    const normalized = normalizeMemo(memo);
    return token && normalized ? { ...token, memo: normalized } : token;
  }

  async execute(
    operation: PreparedSendOperation,
    options?: ExecuteSendOptions,
  ): Promise<{ operation: PendingSendOperation; token: Token }> {
    // existing setup...

    const result = await handler.execute(ctx);

    if (result.status === 'PENDING') {
      const tokenWithMemo = applyTokenMemo(result.token ?? result.pending.token, options?.memo);

      const pendingWithMemo: PendingSendOperation = tokenWithMemo
        ? { ...result.pending, token: tokenWithMemo }
        : result.pending;

      await this.sendOperationRepository.update(pendingWithMemo);
      pending = pendingWithMemo;
      token = tokenWithMemo ?? null;
    }

    // existing failed/missing-token checks...

    await this.eventBus.emit('send:pending', {
      mintUrl: pending.mintUrl,
      operationId: pending.id,
      operation: pending,
      token,
    });

    return { operation: pending, token };
  }
```
  No database schema change should be needed because tokenJson already persists the full token object.

  ## Acceptance Criteria

  - manager.ops.send.execute(operationOrId, { memo: 'hello' }) returns token.memo === 'hello'.
  - The persisted send operation stores the memo-bearing token in tokenJson.
  - manager.history.getPaginatedHistory(...) returns the send entry with entry.token.memo === 'hello'.
  - Whitespace-only memo is treated as omitted.
  - Existing callers of execute(operationOrId) continue working unchanged.
  - Existing send operations without memo remain unchanged.
  - Both default sends and non-default send handlers, such as P2PK, preserve the memo on the persisted token.

  ## Tests

  Add or update tests in:

  - packages/core/test/unit/SendOpsApi.test.ts
  - packages/core/test/unit/SendOperationService.test.ts
  - packages/core/test/unit/HistoryService.test.ts or repository/history projection tests

  Example coverage:
```
  const prepared = await manager.ops.send.prepare({ mintUrl, amount: 1 });
  const { token } = await manager.ops.send.execute(prepared.id, { memo: 'hello' });

  expect(token.memo).toBe('hello');

  const history = await manager.history.getPaginatedHistory(0, 10);
  const sendEntry = history.find((entry) => entry.type === 'send');

  expect(sendEntry?.token?.memo).toBe('hello');

  Whitespace-only memo should not persist:

  const prepared = await manager.ops.send.prepare({ mintUrl, amount: 1 });
  const { token } = await manager.ops.send.execute(prepared.id, { memo: '   ' });

  expect(token.memo).toBeUndefined();

  const history = await manager.history.getPaginatedHistory(0, 10);
  const sendEntry = history.find((entry) => entry.type === 'send');

  expect(sendEntry?.token?.memo).toBeUndefined();
```
  Also add a service-level test that the send:pending event receives the memo-bearing token, because that event is emitted after persistence and drives the history
  projection path.
